Subject: gfx_opengl: highp, not mediump, in the ES shaders

Audit patches P2 and P3 (docs/substrate-audit.md 1.4), two lines.

`precision mediump float;` is emitted into BOTH generated shaders when the
context is ES. On every Apple GPU mediump is fp16. In the vertex shader that
is gl_Position and the interpolated texture coordinates computed at half
precision, and ESSL 3.00's own default there is highp, so the line makes
things strictly worse than saying nothing. In the fragment shader the line
cannot simply be deleted (ESSL leaves fragment float undeclared-by-default)
but it has to say highp: the stretched-edge clamp computes 0.5/texSize, and
an XBLA record at the 4096 cap makes that 1.2e-4 - below fp16's resolution
next to a coordinate near 1.0, i.e. visible smearing on the largest tiles.

diff --git a/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp b/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp
index ccc08fa02..7ca66e188 100644
--- a/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp
+++ b/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp
@@ -285,7 +285,10 @@ static struct ShaderProgram* gfx_opengl_create_and_load_new_shader(uint64_t shad
     vs_len += sprintf(vs_buf + vs_len, "#version %s\n", gl_glsl_version_str);
 
     if (gl_es) {
-        append_line(vs_buf, &vs_len, "precision mediump float;");
+        // highp, not mediump: mediump is fp16 on every Apple GPU, and this is
+        // the shader that computes gl_Position and interpolates the texture
+        // coordinates. ESSL 3.00's own default for vertex float is highp.
+        append_line(vs_buf, &vs_len, "precision highp float;");
     }
 
     if (gl_glsl_version >= 130) {
@@ -388,7 +391,11 @@ static struct ShaderProgram* gfx_opengl_create_and_load_new_shader(uint64_t shad
     fs_len += sprintf(fs_buf + fs_len, "#version %s\n", gl_glsl_version_str);
 
     if (gl_es) {
-        append_line(fs_buf, &fs_len, "precision mediump float;");
+        // Fragment float has no default in ESSL, so the line has to stay, but
+        // it has to say highp: XBLA texture records go up to 4096 across
+        // (xblatex.c XBLATEX_MAXDIM), and texEdge's 0.5/texSize is then 1.2e-4,
+        // which fp16 cannot resolve next to a coordinate near 1.0.
+        append_line(fs_buf, &fs_len, "precision highp float;");
     }
 
     if (gl_glsl_version >= 130) {
